  "generated_text": "1. **Identify the area of one square**: The total area of the region is 294 square centimeters, and it is formed by six congruent squares. Therefore, the area of one square is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{294}{6} = 49 \\text{ square centimeters}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the side length of one square**: Since the area of one square is 49 square centimeters, the side length of each square is:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{49} = 7 \\text{ centimeters}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the perimeter of the region**: The perimeter of the region is the sum of the lengths of all its sides. From the diagram, we can see that the region is formed by 12 sides of the squares. Therefore, the perimeter of the region is:\n   \\[\n   12 \\times 7 = 84 \\text{ centimeters}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Conclusion**: The perimeter of the region is $\\boxed{84}$ centimeters.",
